{title: 169 - Come, You Faithful}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #169 • ST. KEVIN • 7.5.6.7.6.6.6}
{lyricist: John of Damascus}
{composer: Arthur S. Sulllivan}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 169}
{meta: tune ST. KEVIN}
{meta: meter 7.5.6.7.6.6.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F/C]Come, you [C7/Bb]faithful, [Dm/A]raise [F/C]the [C7]strain
[Dm/A]Of triumphant [F/C]gladness;
[F/C]God [C]has [Em/B]brought His [Gm]people
[C]Now rejoice, Jerusalem,
[C]And with [Gm/Bb]true affection
[F]Welcome [C]in unwearied [F/C]strains
[Dm]Jesus'resurrection.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F/C]'Tis the [C7/Bb]spring of [Dm/A]souls [F/C]today;
[Dm/A]Christ has [C]burst [F/C]His prison
[F/C]From [C]the [Em/B]frost and [Gm]gloom of [Em/B]death
[C]light and life have [B7]risen
[C]All the winter of [B7]our [G7/B]sins,
[C]Long and [Gm/Bb]dark, is flying
[F]From His ligth, [C]to whom [F/C]we give
[Dm]Thanks and [C7]praise [Bb]undying.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F/C]"Alleluia!" [Dm/A]now [F/C]we [C7]cry
[Dm/A]to our [C]King [F/C]immortal,
[F/C]Who, [C]triumphant, [Gm]burst the
[C]bars of the tomb's dark [B7]portal
[C]"Alleluia!" with [B7]the [G7/B]Son,
[C]God the [Gm/Bb]Father praising;
[F]"Alleluia!" [C]yet again [F/C]to
[Dm]the Spirit [Bb]raising.
{end_of_verse}
